    ],
    "explanation": "Nazeebo requires to rotate between two lanes in order to gather stacks for Voodoo Ritual as quickly as possible and eventually unlock Vile Infection at Level 20. As a consequence, he is good on Maps where it is fast and safe to rotate between lanes (such as rotating mid-top on Tomb of the Spider Queen) and he should not be picked on Maps where it is impossible to rotate because there are only 2 lanes (like Braxis Holdout), where it is slow and/or dangerous to rotate between lanes (for example Cursed Hollow), or on mid-game Maps where there is a low chance to reach Level 20 (such as Sky Temple)."
  },
  "builds": [
    {
      "name": "Zombie Wall Build",
      "label": "Recommended",
      "description": "Nazeebo's Zombie Wall Build combines a bit more safety with high damage output against enemy Heroes who cannot play around Zombie Wall by using their own Abilities or with the help of allied Heroes.\n\nThe increased casting range provided by Thing of the Deep at Level 1 helps Nazeebo hit enemies with his Abilities—especially Zombie Wall—and gives him extra safety at any stage of the game, unless dove.\n\nWhile his early game damage is not that great, the additional Spell Power provided empowers both his Heroic Abilities, something that will compensate this little weakness during big team fights in the later stages of the game.\n\nAttention! Once you reach Level 20, if you are too far from having 175 stacks of Voodoo Ritual, do not pick Vile Infection because it would do nothing. Upgrade your Heroic Ability instead.",
